BUSINESS INSIGHTS SUMMARY REPORT (EDA)

OBJECTIVE
The objective of this analysis was to evaluate marketing campaign performance across different channels and identify which channels should receive increased budget allocation based on return on investment (ROI), revenue generation, and conversion efficiency.

DATA CLEANING
The dataset was examined for missing values and duplicate records. No major data quality issues were identified, ensuring reliable analysis results.

FUNNEL ANALYSIS
The marketing funnel revealed a significant reduction in customer volume from Impressions to Clicks, followed by further decreases from Clicks to Leads and Leads to Conversions. This indicates that while campaigns successfully generate visibility, there are opportunities to improve engagement and conversion effectiveness.

CHANNEL PERFORMANCE ANALYSIS
Average ROI was calculated for each marketing channel. Search and Email marketing demonstrated the highest ROI values, indicating stronger returns on marketing investment. Display and Influencer channels performed moderately, while Social campaigns generated comparatively lower ROI.
Revenue analysis showed that high-performing channels also contributed significantly to total revenue generation, reinforcing their effectiveness.
Conversion rate analysis provided additional insight into channel efficiency by measuring the percentage of clicks that resulted in conversions. Channels with higher conversion rates demonstrated stronger customer acquisition performance.

RECOMMENDATIONS
Based on ROI, revenue, and conversion performance:
Increase budget allocation for Search and Email marketing campaigns.
Maintain investment levels for Display and Influencer channels while monitoring performance trends.
Reevaluate Social media campaign strategies to improve audience targeting and conversion effectiveness.
Focus on reducing funnel drop-offs through improved ad creatives, landing page optimization, and stronger call-to-action strategies.

CONLCUSION
The analysis indicates that Search and Email channels deliver the strongest overall performance and should receive additional marketing budget. Improving conversion efficiency across the funnel can further enhance campaign effectiveness and maximize return on marketing investment.
